            <ArticleTitle>MRI interaction with tattoo pigments: case report, pathophysiology, and management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1717-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is reported in which the presence of a decorative tattoo resulted in pain and termination of an MRI study. The ferromagnetic nature of the tattoo and iron oxide tattoo pigments is demonstrated. The pathophysiology of tattoo/MRI interaction is discussed, as is an approach to the prevention and treatment of this complication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
